The con in Leicester is only on every two years, so we wanted to do it there, we&#39;d unfortunatly have to wait til July 2016, as we just had one last year. I&#39;d be up for that, at any rate, as it would only require a minimum of effort on my part, and we have the space, etc.&nbsp;

Running a UK tournament this year would be a bit of a challenge, because two of the three conventions (UK Games Expo and Nine Worlds) that would probably be suitable are already too soon/booked out, respectively. Dragonmeet isn&#39;t, but I&#39;d have to ask the guys what the conditions are like for a tournament table. All depends on the likely turnout, obviously.

Honestly, if you want it done this year, renting out a pub for a weekend would probably be the easiest thing to do.&nbsp;
